    "name": "Ho mi Zi (asian mustard heads)",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Ho Mi Zi, also known as Dragon Tongue Mustard, is&nbsp;a variety of Brassica juncea, a type of Asian mustard.&nbsp;It's characterized by its green and purple crinkled leaves with thick white midribs.&nbsp;Young leaves are tender and delicious raw in salads, while mature leaves offer a spicy-sweet flavor suitable for stir-fries.</span></p>",
